# SQL migrations are immutable

Once a migration under `chotu-common/migrations/` is committed, **do not modify it** — even comments.

sqlx stores a SHA-384 checksum of each applied migration. Editing an existing file causes:

`migration … was previously applied but has been modified`

## What to do instead

- Schema change → **new** `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.sql` with a later timestamp than the latest migration
- Clarifying docs → put them in the **new** migration’s header, README, or code comments — not in an old file
- Bug in an already-applied migration → ship a **forward** fix migration; do not rewrite history

## Allowed

- Adding brand-new migration files
- Editing a migration only if it has **never** been committed / never applied anywhere (local WIP only)
